      "writtenOn": "2025-01-08T16:51:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m still a bit wary of unconditionally overriding the current opt-outs, as it could be a lot of flag enable/disable revert churn. I would be OK with banning any new usage of the opt-out while we burn down the exception list, but I don\u0027t love the idea of just trying to land this and seeing what breaks, as the breakage can be pretty subtle for a given target.\n\nThat said, would a name like `RELEASE_R8_FORCE_FULL_MODE` or `RELEASE_R8_DEPRECATE_COMPAT_MODE` have the same meaning?",
      "revId": "47c9c1b7d60c42342f5c84082ef34e1198229561",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8e0b9e95_b7d4fc70",
