      "writtenOn": "2025-01-09T13:18:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From what I can tell we only have very few opt-outs. More specifically, it seems to me that these two targets are the only ones that explicitly disables full mode:\n\n```\npackages/modules/AdServices/sdksandbox/SdkSandbox/Android.bp\npackages/modules/Bluetooth/android/app/Android.bp\n```\n\nInstead of adding a single feature flag to switch these two targets, what if we did one feature flag per build, `RELEASE_R8_FULL_MODE_FOR_BLUETOOTH` and `RELEASE_R8_FULL_MODE_FOR_SDK_SANDBOX`?\n\nI realize that we may need to add more explicit opt-outs as a side effect of enabling R8 full mode by default, but we can tackle those separately.\n\nRegarding `SdkSandbox`, I did come across b/293177283. I also tried running the tests that led us to enable compatibility mode for this target, and they seem to succeed on main with R8 full mode enabled (https://android-build.corp.google.com/abtd/run/L65200030008723828/).",
      "parentUuid": "9df11a1f_7fad65a9",
      "revId": "47c9c1b7d60c42342f5c84082ef34e1198229561",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
